            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Assassination</strong><br>\nOn November 4, 1995, Rabin was assassinated by a right-wing Israeli who opposed the Oslo Accords. His death was a tragic blow to the peace process and shocked the nation and the world.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Memory</strong><br>\nRabin's legacy is remembered for his military leadership, political courage, and his quest for peace. Annual commemorations honor his memory and continue to inspire discussions about peace in the Middle East.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Education and Reflections in History Books</strong><br>\nRabin's life and work are now part of history education, teaching new generations about the complexities of leadership, the pain of conflict, and the enduring hope for peace. His story is a powerful tool for educators to discuss the importance of diplomacy and mutual understanding.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
